; DOMAIN: bsd-formula [CLOSED, derived 2026-07-25]
; Claim: The full Birch-Swinnerton-Dyer leading-coefficient formula for E/Q of analytic/algebraic rank r. Assuming L(E,s) has order of vanishing r at s=1 (the ord=rank statement is genesis_bsd_conjecture at GENESIS 122), the leading Taylor coefficient is L^(r)(E,1)/r! = (#Sha(E/Q) * Omega_E * Reg_E * prod_p c_p) / (#E(Q)_tors)^2, where #Sha(E/Q) is the (conjecturally finite) order of the Tate-Shafarevich group, Omega_E the real period (integral over E(R) of |omega| for the Neron differential), Reg_E the regulator (det of the Neron-Tate height-pairing Gram matrix on a Z-basis of E(Q)/tors), prod_p c_p the product of Tamagawa numbers over primes of bad reduction, and #E(Q)_tors the order of the torsion subgroup. This is the explicit leading-coefficient assembly node tying together all five durable component nodes; it is scale-correct under the Neron differential normalization (Omega archimedean vs Reg algebraic). Bridge: genesis_real_period (Omega_E) + genesis_regulator (Reg_E) + genesis_tamagawa_number (prod_p c_p) + genesis_sha_group (#Sha) + genesis_l_function_elliptic (L^(r)(E,1)/r! target).
(= (bsd-formula $E) (equal (div (nth-derivative (l-function $E) (rank $E) 1) (factorial (rank $E))) (div (times (times (times (order (sha $E)) (real-period $E)) (regulator $E)) (tamagawa-product $E)) (square (order (torsion $E))))))
(= (bsd-leading-coeff-numerator $E) (times (times (times (order (sha $E)) (real-period $E)) (regulator $E)) (tamagawa-product $E)))
(= (bsd-leading-coeff-denominator $E) (square (order (torsion $E))))
(= (tamagawa-product $E) (product-over-bad-primes (tamagawa-number $E)))
(= (bsd-formula-assembles $E) (list (real-period $E) (regulator $E) (tamagawa-product $E) (order (sha $E)) (order (torsion $E)))))